# apps/control-panel/Dockerfile.dockerignore -- the build context of the control panel image, and ONLY of it.
#
# BuildKit reads `<Dockerfile name>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile in place of the root .dockerignore, for
# that one Dockerfile. This image copies the whole repository into its builder stage (`COPY . /codemap-src`) so
# that the code map can be made from the code, and a copy of everything must not carry a secret. So this file is
# an ALLOW-LIST: the first line excludes everything, the next lines let the source folders back in, and the
# last lines exclude again what must never be in a build context. Secrets never enter this context: the last lines
# drop a `secrets` folder at any depth (the operator's, and k8s/overlays/production/secrets), every `.env*` and
# `*.env` file, key and certificate files, and the generated livekit.prod.yaml. They mirror what .gitignore marks
# as secret; when .gitignore gains a new secret path, add it here too (dockerignore.test.mjs checks the list).
# A new top-level folder stays out until it is added here.
#
# The legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0) ignores this file and applies the root .dockerignore: the code map then
# reads its commit as "unknown" and has fewer L0 files, and nothing fails (apps/control-panel/codemap/README.md).
*

!apps
!compose
!docker
!docker-compose*.yml
!gremion-public
!gremion-ui
!infra
!k8s
!modules
!ops
!packages
!services
!scripts
!test
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml

# the commit, without a git program: HEAD, and the refs that HEAD can point at
!.git/HEAD
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs

**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
**/build
**/coverage
gremion-ui/_module-lane
**/.env*
**/*.env
**/*.env.local
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets
docker/livekit/livekit.prod.yaml
